<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka NDB to convert debentures.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka NDB to convert debentures.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lankan blue chip development finance institution National Development Bank Ltd said on Wednesday it would convert 27.5 million debentures into shares in August and start floating them on the Colombo Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>NDB, which has an issued capital of 17.5 million 10-rupee shares, has issued 27.5 million convertible debentures of 10 rupees each to the government of Sri Lanka (GOSL), a company statement said.</p>
</text>
